TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) adding the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  Yeah, there are a lot of chords here but they're all easy.  The intro is a bit jumpy with single strums of the (C)(Bm)(Am)(G).  For (Dsus2) just lift off the 1st string from the (D).  

There's a single (Bm) in the chorus that's only played once so expect it and it'll be no problem.  The (E)-(Esus) in the bridge is simple as you're already playing the (E) so just add your pinky below your ring finger.


